Breaks: A send that was refused still reports a message to anything parsing the answer, so a terminal command prints a message it never sent: the handler attaches what it got before checking the error, and a refusal no longer drops it.
Must fail: go test ./internal/mcpserver -run '^TestARefusalCarriesNothingToParse$' -count=1

